RELEASE_CANDIDATE

Version `2.0.0-rc.1` is the first 2.0 release-candidate development baseline.

The 2.0 line introduces native Codex and Claude Code host adapters, the unified
Python `governance.py` management interface, host-neutral governed-project
lifecycle handling, ownership-safe host configuration, and removal of the
legacy PowerShell/shell management entrypoints.

The frozen GOV-001..030 scenario definitions and scoring rubrics remain
unchanged. Candidate behavioral acceptance requires independently scored,
complete campaigns on both supported agent hosts: Codex and Claude Code.

Claude Code behavioral testing has now been performed: all 30 scenarios were
captured and independently assessed at 49/60, below the required 58/60
threshold. This is failed behavioral-evaluation evidence, not acceptance.
That campaign used an earlier runner context; a fresh independently scored
30-scenario campaign using the current native host-adapter runner is still
required before candidate acceptance.

A protected GitHub-hosted Ubuntu workflow is prepared to produce that fresh
Claude Code campaign and its seven-day independent scoring packet. It has not
yet been executed as full-campaign evidence.

Behavioral acceptance and exact-commit cross-platform assurance are not yet
complete. Version `1.0.0` remains the latest published stable release.

No commit, tag, push, release, or publication is authorized by this status.
